Package: propsens
Type: Package
Title: Propensity Model Sensitivity Diagnostics for Matched Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-11-12
Authors@R: person(given = "Mostafa M.", family = "Abbas",
                  email = "mostafa.mn.abbas@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Outcome-free diagnostics of how much a matched design depends
    on which of several similarly good propensity models is used. Logistic
    regression, Bayesian additive regression trees and a generalized random
    forest (cross-fitted scores) are each used for 1:1 nearest-neighbour
    matching with the analyst's settings; a quality gate keeps the models that
    fit and balance about as well as the best one, and the package reports
    study-level rank disagreement, pair instability, bootstrap rank
    instability of the logistic model and balance spread across the kept
    models. It reads an existing 'MatchIt' object directly. The diagnostics
    have been studied in the author's simulations; no peer-reviewed evaluation
    exists yet.
